  "findings": [
    "The UI-disabled baseline (same busy scene, no UI node) reaches 14.2\u201316.0 ms p95 in five of six runs; one OpenGL run measured 7.9 ms for that first workload only.",
    "Workloads with the UI active sit within about \u00b11.5 ms of each run's own UI-disabled baseline (the +8.8 ms outlier is the OpenGL run whose baseline measured 7.9 ms); UI API CPU p95 never exceeds 1.61 ms and core CPU never exceeds 0.82 ms.",
    "All eight failing checks are OpenGL and exceed the limit by 0.04\u20130.41 ms, less than the run-to-run spread of the UI-disabled baseline itself.",
    "The 16.667 ms whole-frame limit therefore leaves under 1 ms for the UI in this scene; the failures measure scene plus presentation cost, with no UI-attributable regression visible in the data."
